# Mishthi Sattva — server environment variables
#
# These are set in VERCEL (Project → Settings → Environment Variables), never
# in this repo. This file lists the NAMES and where each value comes from, so
# the site can be rebuilt from scratch without guesswork.
#
# ⚠️  NEVER put the real values in any file in this repository — not here, not
#     in js/config.js, not in a comment. Two of them below can drain money or
#     expose every customer's phone number and address. Anything committed to
#     git is permanent, and anything in js/config.js is downloaded by every
#     visitor's browser.
#
# Copy this to .env.local for local API testing (.env* is gitignored).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED — without this the site cannot record orders at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase → Settings → API → "service_role" (click to reveal).
# Bypasses every row-level security policy, which is exactly why it lives on
# the server only. It is what lets /api write orders now that the browser's
# permission to do so has been removed (see supabase/orders-payments.sql).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to the project URL hard-coded in api/_lib.mjs; set it only
# if the Supabase project ever moves.
SUPABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONLINE PAYMENTS — until both are set, "Pay online" is hidden at checkout
# rather than shown and failing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Razorpay Dashboard → Settings → API Keys.
# The key ID is public by design (it is sent to the browser to open checkout).
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=

# The secret is NOT public. It signs every payment; verifying that signature is
# the only thing that proves money actually arrived.
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CASH ON DELIVERY — a business decision, so it is its own switch. Set to the
# literal string "true" to offer COD at checkout; leave unset to hide it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENABLE_COD=
